    "specPath": "specs/035-screening-seam/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved specs 002, 003 and 009, for #76 child B7 (#65). A definition may declare a `screening` block that names untrusted text fields (caller text, third-party text, list item text), the screener backend that judges each one, a consequence on block (`refuse`, `drop_field`, `drop_text`, `drop_item`) and a consequence when the screener is unavailable (`fail_closed`, `skip_generation`, `fail_open`). The block compiles down to ordinary `proposition` steps, one text value per request, plus consequence rules evaluated before the selection policy; a screener is an ordinary backend that declares a `screen` profile (categories, maximum text bytes, text unit size) and uses the general per-capability `isolation: per_item` member this spec introduces. In a definition that declares screening, the compiler refuses a model step that reads unscreened untrusted text. A blocked value under `refuse` yields spec 033's `refused` outcome with its computed addressing. Adds a `screen_unavailable` unresolved reason, an explicit withheld marker in projections, per-value screening evidence with digests only, text-unit budgets, verdict caching through spec 017's cache, the reserved `rustev.screening` metric of spec 028, a per-item isolation rule for spec 009 remote adapters, and the mapping constraints for spec 030's reserved Bedrock screening values. New members go into the shared #76 track versions (`rustev.definition/2`, `rustev.plan/3`, `rustev.evidence/2`, `rustev.judgment/2`, `rustev.run/3`); definitions, descriptors and plans that use no #76 construct keep byte-identical identities. Approved (A-32); implementation is in progress.\n",
    "title": "Untrusted-text screening seam (amends 002, 003 and 009)"
  },
